\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Form C made visible. A per-sector additive shift translates each sector's velocity block along the scalar axis. Where the shift happens to land a block on a node, a large fraction of the domain ``locks'' at once --- not because the velocities are harmonically structured, but because the normalization moved them there. The lock is an artifact of the preprocessing, not a property of the stars.}}{7}{figure.1.1}\protected@file@percent }
