\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {chapter}{\numberline {2}The Verdict on L1\_GWTC: The Right Observable, Too Few Events}{10}{chapter.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\addvspace {10\p@ }}
\@writefile{lot}{\addvspace {10\p@ }}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {2.1}What the Lake Was Accused Of}{10}{section.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Why the rebuild was necessary. A real ringdown frequency must sit between the non-spinning Kerr floor and the extremal ceiling for its remnant mass. The old frequencies sat \emph  {below} the floor --- physically impossible --- proving they were not the fundamental mode. The rebuilt frequencies, measured $f_{220}$ from LVK posteriors, sit inside the band.}}{10}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
