\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {chapter}{\numberline {12}How the Vector Engine Differs From All Four Before It}{51}{chapter.12}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\addvspace {10\p@ }}
\@writefile{lot}{\addvspace {10\p@ }}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12.1}{\ignorespaces The five engines. The vector engine is the first to leave the line for the sphere, the first whose datum is a vector rather than a scalar, the first to use the number 24 as a set of directions rather than a divisor, and the first whose data is plentiful rather than scarce. It adds two nulls the scalar engines never needed --- the rotation null (a frame question) and the isotropic null (a concentration question) --- while keeping the scramble as the spine.}}{51}{table.12.1}\protected@file@percent }
