\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces Candidate vector targets. Unlike the scalar survey, the limiting quantity is not sample size --- it is systematic anisotropy, named in the last column for each. The pulsar spin--velocity alignment is listed deliberately as a \emph  {known} real alignment: a class the engine must recover, or it is not trustworthy on the cases where the answer is unknown.}}{53}{table.13.1}\protected@file@percent }
